---
// Privacy Policy — truthful disclosure (no image uploads; GA + CF Insights)
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Privacy Policy — Low Quality Image Maker';
const description = 'How Low Quality Image Maker handles your data: images are processed entirely in your browser and never uploaded, plus full disclosure of the analytics we use.';
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description}>
  <nav class="sticky top-0 z-50 bg-white/80 backdrop-blur-xl border-b border-zinc-200">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 h-16 flex items-center justify-between">
      <a href="https://www.low-quality-image-maker.com" class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-800 hover:text-zinc-900 transition-colors">← Back to the image maker</a>
      <span class="text-xs text-zinc-600 font-mono uppercase tracking-wider">Privacy</span>
    </div>
  </nav>
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 md:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tighter text-zinc-900">Privacy <span class="text-brand-700">Policy</span></h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-600">Last updated: September 22, 2026</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">Your images never leave your device</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">
      All image processing happens locally in your browser using the HTML5 Canvas API. When you drop a file into the tool,
      it is read with the browser-native FileReader API and converted with <code class="text-sm text-zinc-800">canvas.toBlob()</code> —
      no image bytes, filenames, or metadata are ever transmitted to our servers, because there is no server component that accepts them.
      You can verify this by opening your browser's Network tab while processing an image.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">Analytics we collect</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">
      To understand which features people use, this site runs two privacy-limited analytics services:
      <strong class="text-zinc-800">Google Analytics</strong> (measurement ID G-PFV7G4GX4L), which collects anonymized page-view and referral information, and
      <strong class="text-zinc-800">Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>, which measures traffic without cookies or browser fingerprinting.
      We do not sell, share, or rent any data to third parties. There are no advertising trackers and no email collection on this site.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">Cookies, storage, and children</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">
      Google Analytics may set a cookie (<code class="text-sm text-zinc-800">_ga</code>) to distinguish returning visitors; you can block it via your browser settings.
      The tool itself stores nothing — no localStorage, no IndexedDB, no service worker cache of your files.
      The site is directed at a general audience, collects no personal information from children, and is not intended to require consent under GDPR beyond the analytics cookie noted above.
      Questions about this policy: email <a href="mailto:hello@low-quality-image-maker.com" class="text-brand-700 hover:text-brand-800 underline underline-offset-2">hello@low-quality-image-maker.com</a> or see the <a href="/about/" class="text-brand-700 hover:text-brand-800 underline underline-offset-2">About page</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
